      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12100672268907563,
        "y0": 0.7958990498812352,
        "x1": 0.8832873949579833,
        "y1": 0.8578942992874109
      },
      "text": "We ﬁrst consider the case v ∈ Σ \\ {p}. Then, K∞,v∞/Kn,vn is the trivial extension or the unramiﬁed Zp-extension. If the extension K∞,v∞/Kn,vn is trivial, then it is clear that Kergn,v± n = 0. Assume that K∞,v∞/Kn,vn is the unramiﬁed Zp-extension. Write Bv∞ := E[p∞]GK∞,v∞ . We consider the exact sequence",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
